    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d166">

                <pb facs="0506" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d166-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-29">29 June, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To President from Former Naval Person personal and secret. Number 336.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d166-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I should be very glad to arrange for a meeting between us and our staffs about
                    the end of August in Quebec which I am sure Mackenzie King would welcome. Later
                    on I will put the point to him.</p>
                <p>Many thanks for your very full message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d166-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d166-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission not indicated.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d166-f2" n="2" xml:id="d166-f2-content">
                <p>For the paragraph omitted here, see <ref target="frus1943CairoTehran#pg_13">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conferences at Cairo and
                        Tehran, 1943, p. 13</ref>.</p>
            </note>
